  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Alabama's federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date are $113M. The Federal government awarded 223 contracts in the state, with an average award size of $508K. Obligations are down 99.3% year over year. Historical context shows prior fiscal years with much larger totals: FY22 was $14.1B, FY23 was $14.9B, FY24 was $17.3B, FY25 was $18.1B, and FY26 was $17.2B. The Department of Veterans Affairs leads buying in FY2027 to date with $84.6M, followed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $22.8M and the Department of Justice with $3.9M. AMERESCO INC is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $52.3M, followed by PINTER MEMORIALS INC with $17.9M and AMENTUM TECHNOLOGY, INC. with $10.5M. Engineering Services is the top industry in FY2027 to date at $54.2M, followed by Cut Stone and Stone Product Manufacturing at $16.7M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $11.7M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial.",
